{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf","id":548379,"title":"Beast vs Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-10T05:31:06-07:00","id":548379,"title":"Beast vs Werewolf","content":"Some people have been saying that Beasts are overpowered. I'm trying to get a sense if this is true or not. Has anyone sat down and done a point by point comparison to see which one comes out in the lead? I don't mean a white room combat against each other, but two characters being built towards the same role and seeing which one is better.<br /> <br /> Combat?<br /> Tracking?<br /> Social?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:33:11-07:00","id":548441,"title":"","content":"I can't see why anyone would, the games aren't balanced across splats, so it's not as if Beast was supposed to be just as powerful as werewolf and no more. Beast is supposed to be as powerful as Beast.<br /> <br /> If you want to know how the Beast abilities work, the doc is available on the Kickstarter page. People talking about overpowered stuff might be referring to some of the Atavisms, many of which require no roll or cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:01:53-07:00","id":548463,"title":"","content":"I'd expect anyone with a crossover-friendly game in mind to pay a <i>little </i>more attention to that sort of thing though. Balance is probably still an illusion, but I would hope it's fakeness attribute has taken a knock in this specific environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:13:04-07:00","id":548472,"title":"","content":"(For the record, this is my first foray back into the forums in at least a year, so I haven't seen a lot of the discussions you're referencing yet.)<br /> <br /> I think the impression of Beast as overpowered probably comes from a small handful of things:<br /> <br /> * They get the ability to recognize other splats as an inherent power, and can kiiiiinda con other splats into thinking they're one as well.<br /> * Their Skeleton Key power to doorkick their way into another splat's special dimension.<br /> * Combat applicability of a few specific powers.<br /> * Battlefield control via manifestation of part or all of their Lair.<br /> <br /> In a knowledge-is-power sense, the Beasts initially seem to have a colossal advantage over the other splats, but the lack of a central 'secret society' of any kind means that mostly they don't know the first thing about the critter they've run into other than the fact it isn't a vanilla human.<br /> <br /> I haven't sat down and actually done extensive number crunching on the subject, but my impression from having read 95ish % of the text is that Beasts are about on equal footing with their cousins in most ways. Pretty much like all of the splats, they have specific situations where they're at a massive advantage against most potential enemies. A combat specced giant in hand to hand combat with an unarmed foe, for instance, will have a serious strength advantage and a kraken will have a huge upper hand in a grappling contest but there's also things that they simply can't do. In a head-to-head with a social-specialized Vampire they're at a huge disadvantage simply because they lack any sort of mind control powers. In terms of post-combat recovery the Uratha make Beasts look like chemo patients by comparison.<br /> <br /> * Vampires can control minds and turn invisible (among other things, obv.). Beasts can't. Edit: I stand corrected, they actually CAN turn invisible.<br /> <br /> * Werewolves regenerate from virtually all injuries at staggering speeds. Beasts don't. Even their high speed healing power is like molasses by comparison, and active healing of anything but bashing damage is relatively costly. Edit Two: aaaand apparently I'm mis-remembering the Werewolf regeneration rules by a bit. Mea Culpa.<br /> <br /> * Beasts don't inherently take aggravated damage from much of anything BUT if they get tagged by a Hero virtually anything might develop the ability to cripple them.<br /> <br /> * Mages can conjure roaring columns of lightning and fire from the skies or boil you alive with a Word. Beasts can breathe fire, which they cannot subsequently control.<br /> <br /> * A Beast can (sometimes) manipulate a battlefield to their advantage by leveraging their Lair, but a Geist using the Boneyard powers has similar capabilities with more flexibility and fewer prerequisites.<br /> <br /> * Beasts' Nightmare powers sound potentially unbalancing, but you have to remember that they're really only an unopposed check against a normal person.<br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR: I'm pretty sure people are reacting more to the combination of Shiny New Powerz and excellent flavor text than they are to the actual concrete mechanics of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":1647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","user":"Mechalith","date":". 06-10-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:29:01-07:00","id":548542,"title":"","content":"Beasts <i>can</i> turn invisible. It's the satiety expenditure effect of From the Shadows. <br /> <br /> The healing factor granted by Relentless hunter is equal to that of a low primal urge werewolf with regards to bashing, worse than a werewolf for lethal and slightly <i>better</i> than a werewolf for aggravated, healing a dot every 3 days rather than 4. With satiety expenditure they can heal at gauru rate for a turn, and get rid of aggravated entirely, which werewolves just can't do at will. In their lair they're basically healing everything all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:51:22-07:00","id":548545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548542#post548542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts <i>can</i> turn invisible. It's the satiety expenditure effect of From the Shadows.<br /> <br /> The healing factor granted by Relentless hunter is equal to that of a low primal urge werewolf with regards to bashing, worse than a werewolf for lethal and slightly <i>better</i> than a werewolf for aggravated, healing a dot every 3 days rather than 4. With satiety expenditure they can heal at gauru rate for a turn, and get rid of aggravated entirely, which werewolves just can't do at will. In their lair they're basically healing everything all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected (and edited my initial post accordingly). I stand behind the general thrust of the post though. Any given critter has advantages and disadvantages in specific situations.<br /> <br /> As to your earlier point as to whether a crossover specific game should be more interested in balance: There's an actual section in the Beast book labeled &quot;Game Balance?&quot; which (heavily paraphrased) essentially says that the objective potential power balance doesn't and shouldn't matter. It contends that the important thing is that you don't have one or more players feeling slighted because someone decided to be a jerk and powergame over the top of their character concept. Need to balance against a particular NPC threat? Chances are, they have numbers and organization in their favor. Need to worry about PVP balance for some obnoxious reason or other? That's up to the PCs to figure out. If there's one jerk in the group who likes to grab the most powerful option and bully the other characters then it's up to the Storyteller to contain their BS or (preferably) kick them from the game and replace them with someone who isn't a complete prick.<br /> <br /> I tend to agree with the author. Trying to balance every game mechanic against every other is not only futile, it pretty much misses the point of telling a crossover story IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:56:52-07:00","id":548550,"title":"","content":"Whoever is cleverer with what they have is the superior animal.<br /> <br /> ....But I do feel like werewolves have the advantage, what with a focus on claiming environments for themselves and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-10-2015, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:08:36-07:00","id":548566,"title":"","content":"Also Beasts can get a lot of armor, including armor vs Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> One of their Atavisms would essentially allow a Beast to kill most of a pack, then confront the survivors afterwards and they wouldn't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:47:36-07:00","id":548705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548472#post548472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't sat down and actually done extensive number crunching on the subject, but my impression from having read 95ish % of the text is that Beasts are about on equal footing with their cousins in most ways. Pretty much like all of the splats, they have specific situations where they're at a massive advantage against most potential enemies. A combat specced giant in hand to hand combat with an unarmed foe, for instance, will have a serious strength advantage and a kraken will have a huge upper hand in a grappling contest but there's also things that they simply can't do. In a head-to-head with a social-specialized Vampire they're at a huge disadvantage simply because they lack any sort of mind control powers. In terms of post-combat recovery the Uratha make Beasts look like chemo patients by comparison.<br /> <br /> * Vampires can control minds and turn invisible (among other things, obv.). Beasts can't. Edit: I stand corrected, they actually CAN turn invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts can also control minds with You Must Obey, wipe memories with Tabula Rasa, etc...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:08:43-07:00","id":548775,"title":"","content":"Vampires are social predators and control freaks.<br /> Werewolves are hunters and masters of their territory.<br /> Mages are academics and scientists, creatures of intellect and the mind.<br /> Prometheans are (post-apocalytic-type) survivors.<br /> Changelings are illusionists, wish/dream granters, and abusers.<br /> Hunters are batman, average people doing the best humanity can.<br /> Bound are, well, I want to say street-gang-like, dealing with death and curses.<br /> Mummies are youngsters growing old and their bodies failing them, but getting wiser<br /> Demons are stealthy spy types. <br /> Beasts... haven't finished the book, so I can't say.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my point is that every supernatural has its strong point (and, ironically, its also their weak points). In those specific area, the supernatural in question reigns supreme. I don't care how many dots in Mind a mage has, he really can't beat vampires with their powers of mind control. The mage will never be better at territory control or hunting than a werewolf, illusions/dreams as a 'ling, etc. Mages need to study and prepare to be as good in a field; while they can do a lot, they're not too hot without that preparation or specific knowledge.<br /> <br /> And so it goes for everyone. Vampire versus werewolf. Demon versus changeling. You name it. If we can play to one group's strengths but not another's, then the one we're playing to generally will win. <br /> <br /> So, when people are comparing Beasts to werewolves, they're seeing the wolves having to play in the Beast's strengths. Not surprisingly, since Beast the game is written from that perspective. In a hunt? The wolves are far better off. Always will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:11:42-07:00","id":548779,"title":"","content":"Meh. Demons pwn everybody else! ;p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:40:03-07:00","id":548814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548566#post548566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Beasts can get a lot of armor, including armor vs Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> One of their Atavisms would essentially allow a Beast to kill most of a pack, then confront the survivors afterwards and they wouldn't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one is that?<br /> Both the Siren's Song one and the Dragonfire one aren't that powerful (though Dragonfire being a Reflexive actions is over the top and I am operating under the assumption that this is a mistake).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:52:46-07:00","id":548837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548814#post548814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which one is that?<br /> Both the Siren's Song one and the Dragonfire one aren't that powerful (though Dragonfire being a Reflexive actions is over the top and I am operating under the assumption that this is a mistake).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alien Allure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:14:00-07:00","id":548933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548705#post548705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can also control minds with You Must Obey, wipe memories with Tabula Rasa, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just not my day for remembering things accurately. I was thinking of the bit in the Atavism section that says &quot;The one thing Atavisms cannot do is directly control someone\u2019s mind.&quot; When I first read the You Must Obey text, I assumed (because I was still skimming) that the Nightmare was just an illusion, a vision where the character is forced to do terrible things that do not objectively happen in the rest of the world. On re-reading, it appears that you're correct and it does function essentially like Dominate.<br /> <br /> As far as the bit about killing an entire pack and the rest of them being fine with it afterward, that doesn't seem to be how the Alien Allure power is intended to work. For starters, it only affects how you behave toward the user, not how you feel about what they may have done when they aren't present. Also, while it says after a day without contact 'all is forgiven' for purposes of social maneuvering, it doesn't mean that you <i>literally</i> forgive them, only that you're not holding it against them in conversation at the moment. And finally, for it to work at all they're going to have to beat you in a Clash of Wills/resistance roll, because while <i>most</i> of the Atavisms don't do things where it would be applicable, that situation definitely calls for it. (For purposes of discussion, I'm not getting into whether of not a socially inclined Beast is going to be able to take down a whole pack of werewolves.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":1647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","user":"Mechalith","date":".  Edited to correct a mid-sentence subject order change that didn't make any sense. 06-10-2015, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:15:56-07:00","id":548935,"title":"","content":"It would be pretty difficult for a Beast to last more than a turn after being applied the Stunned tilt and then being dog-piled by the whole Uratha pack ready to devour it alive, inflicting massive dose of aggravated damage, while at the same time, grappling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:18:21-07:00","id":548941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548837#post548837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alien Allure</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that work to force a Pack to murder each other?<br /> &quot;They are under no compulsion to obey, however, but do feel their job, position, or social standing is at stake if they refuse.&quot;<br /> A werewolf might go along with you and kill their pack. But I think there is a good chance they won't because even if their job/position/social standing were at stake, they won't kill their packmates. As I understand it, packmates mean a lot to each other.<br /> <br /> Just forcing Doors on the Werewolves via the Social Manevering probably won't work either, because you need to state you goal before social maneuvering and &quot;<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">At this point, the Storyteller determines whether the goal <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">is reasonable. A character might, with time and proper tactics, <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">convince a rich person to give him a large sum of money. He <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">probably isn\u2019t going to convince the wealthy individual to <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">abandon <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>all </i><span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of his wealth to the character.&quot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I doubt you will find many STs that would see attempts to talk a Werewolf into killing their packmates as a reasonable goal for Social Maneuvering. Social Maneuvering is not intended to allow you to force actions on a character as if it was mundane Mind Control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 06-10-2015, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:19:41-07:00","id":548944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548814#post548814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which one is that?<br /> Both the Siren's Song one and the Dragonfire one aren't that powerful (though Dragonfire being a Reflexive actions is over the top and I am operating under the assumption that this is a mistake).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Dragonfire is listed as reflexive because you're meant to still have to take an action to blast someone with it, but it doesn't require an action to activate. Probably ought to be clarified in the text, and if I'm wrong it's definitely in need of alteration because that would be absurd. If I'm right then the person who wrote that Atavism essentially did something akin to giving humans the Fist Atavism (that lets you turn your hands into slightly harder hands to better shove them at someone else and harm them on impact) and listed it as reflexive because turning your fist on doesn't take an action but punching someone does. Badly thought out, but not necessarily a balance issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:25:38-07:00","id":548984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548941#post548941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would that work to force a Pack to murder each other?<br /> &quot;They are under no compulsion to obey, however, but do feel their job, position, or social standing is at stake if they refuse.&quot;<br /> A werewolf might go along with you and kill their pack. But I think there is a good chance they won't because even if their job/position/social standing were at stake, they won't kill their packmates. As I understand it, packmates mean a lot to each other.<br /> <br /> Just forcing Doors on the Werewolves via the Social Manevering probably won't work either, because you need to state you goal before social maneuvering and &quot;<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">At this point, the Storyteller determines whether the goal <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">is reasonable. A character might, with time and proper tactics, <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">convince a rich person to give him a large sum of money. He <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">probably isn\u2019t going to convince the wealthy individual to <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">abandon <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><i>all </i><span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of his wealth to the character.&quot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I doubt you will find many STs that would see attempts to talk a Werewolf into killing their packmates as a reasonable goal for Social Maneuvering. Social Maneuvering is not intended to allow you to force actions on a character as if it was mundane Mind Control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty sure that Nofather meant that the Beast could kill most of the pack <i>themselves</i> and then, after the fact, stroll up to the rest of said pack and they would be chill regarding the mass murder of their friends. Even so, your reasoning still applies IMO, in addition to the reasons I've laid out for why it wouldn't work out that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:30:50-07:00","id":548996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548933#post548933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just not my day for remembering things accurately. I was thinking of the bit in the Atavism section that says &quot;The one thing Atavisms cannot do is directly control someone\u2019s mind.&quot; When I first read the You Must Obey text, I assumed (because I was still skimming) that the Nightmare was just an illusion, a vision where the character is forced to do terrible things that do not objectively happen in the rest of the world. On re-reading, it appears that you're correct and it does function essentially like Dominate.<br /> <br /> As far as the bit about killing an entire pack and the rest of them being fine with it afterward, that doesn't seem to be how the Alien Allure power is intended to work. For starters, it only affects how you behave toward the user, not how you feel about what they may have done when they aren't present. Also, while it says after a day without contact 'all is forgiven' for purposes of social maneuvering, it doesn't mean that you <i>literally</i> forgive them, only that they're not holding it against you in conversation at the moment. And finally, for it to work at all they're going to have to beat you in a Clash of Wills/resistance roll, because while <i>most</i> of the Atavisms don't do things where it would be applicable, that situation definitely calls for it. (For purposes of discussion, I'm not getting into whether of not a socially inclined Beast is going to be able to take down a whole pack of werewolves.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mostly right, though Alien Allure can inflict the Charmed condition, and thus change how people feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:31:05-07:00","id":548997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548933#post548933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, for it to work at all they're going to have to beat you in a Clash of Wills/resistance roll, because while <i>most</i> of the Atavisms don't do things where it would be applicable, that situation definitely calls for it. (For purposes of discussion, I'm not getting into whether of not a socially inclined Beast is going to be able to take down a whole pack of werewolves.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills requires another magical ability. It's where two magical abilities clash. There isn't an ability in Werewolf for, 'Remembering that guy who I hate,' and Alien Allure doesn't have a roll to begin with. It's automatic, passive.<br /> <br /> As for socially inclined Beasts, there's actually only two social Atavisms, and the other one is also a weapon. Since you start as a Beast with two Atavisms, it's entirely possible one is going to allow you to kill some werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:45:43-07:00","id":549012,"title":"","content":"One of the things about Beasts is that while they are pretty strong in a few areas, they also have a few holes in their abilities.<br /> For example they have a small number of effects that help with grappling, but really nothing that would allow them to come out on top if a focused Mummy, Werewolf, or Promethean gets their hands on them.<br /> Their best offensive powers are also very specific. Dragonfire for example is powerful, but because fire based attacks are so widespread nearly every splat has one or more powers that would allow them to significantly reduce its potency. A Werewolf with Tongue of Flame could probably do quite a lot to protect their pack from a Dragonfire Beast.<br /> <br /> Other example, do Beasts get any specific defenses against mind influencing effects? Haven't read the book in-depth enough to say for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:46:59-07:00","id":549014,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, a Rahu werewolf with a high presence and intimidate score can stare down a Beast and make them Submissive. And that's before we start getting into Gifts or Form benefits. When it comes to dominance competitions, do not mess with the 'wolves. All I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:47:15-07:00","id":549015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548997#post548997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clash of Wills requires another magical ability. It's where two magical abilities clash. There isn't an ability in Werewolf for, 'Remembering that guy who I hate,' and Alien Allure doesn't have a roll to begin with. It's automatic, passive.<br /> <br /> As for socially inclined Beasts, there's actually only two social Atavisms, and the other one is also a weapon. Since you start as a Beast with two Atavisms, it's entirely possible one is going to allow you to kill some werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's not a gift called Recall the Douchebag, no, but I'd argue that pack loyalty at least falls into the realm of animal instinct and thus Primal Urge. If I were running a game where this came up it'd probably be a contested Presence+Lair vs. Resolve+Primal Urge roll to see if the power had it's intended effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:47:48-07:00","id":549017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549012#post549012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things about Beasts is that while they are pretty strong in a few areas, they also have a few holes in their abilities.<br /> For example they have a small number of effects that help with grappling, but really nothing that would allow them to come out on top if a focused Mummy, Werewolf, or Promethean gets their hands on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they could just toss them very, very far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Werewolf with Tongue of Flame could probably do quite a lot to protect their pack from a Dragonfire Beast. </div> </div> </div>A Beast with Dragonfire is immune to fire damage, and heat or smoke effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:49:27-07:00","id":549018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549015#post549015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a gift called Recall the Douchebag, no, but I'd argue that pack loyalty at least falls into the realm of animal instinct and thus Primal Urge. If I were running a game where this came up it'd probably be a contested Presence+Lair vs. Resolve+Primal Urge roll to see if the power had it's intended effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability specifically calls it out. If you actively hurt someone, give it a day, and they'll forgive you. There's no roll for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:57:25-07:00","id":549023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549017#post549017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Beast with Dragonfire is immune to fire damage, and heat or smoke effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are misunderstanding what I was going for. Protect the Pack <b>from</b> the Dragonfire. Not use Tongue of flames to attack the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:59:40-07:00","id":549026,"title":"","content":"I gotcha, but it's still a nice advantage. You could only defend the others, not turn it against the Beast. And that's the type of conflict that would require a Clash of Wills, since we were on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:01:43-07:00","id":549028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549018#post549018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ability specifically calls it out. If you actively hurt someone, give it a day, and they'll forgive you. There's no roll for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could interpret it to work this way by the literal text, but the intent doesn't seem nearly that extreme. If it IS intended to work the way you think it is then it is absurdly overpowered and badly needs to be re-thought IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:20:17-07:00","id":549042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549028#post549028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose you could interpret it to work this way by the literal text, but the intent doesn't seem nearly that extreme. If it IS intended to work the way you think it is then it is absurdly overpowered and badly needs to be re-thought IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is possible not everyone who claims the abilities are overpowered is completely wrong. Other abilities call out Clash of Wills, most notably the turn invisible one, versus magic senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:29:39-07:00","id":549077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549012#post549012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other example, do Beasts get any specific defenses against mind influencing effects? Haven't read the book in-depth enough to say for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough they're actually more vulnerable if they're full. They can't add Lair to defend from or resist mental influence while they have the Gorged condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:33:01-07:00","id":549092,"title":"","content":"And if they're Slumbering they're basically human. Presumably a tactic to use against Beasts when a werewolf, or anyone, isn't capable of taking them head on would be to sort of trick them into overeating, then kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T12:41:29-07:00","id":549185,"title":"","content":"Then hope their soul doesn't get an exceptional success when they unfetter, because if it does it might hold a grudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:03:59-07:00","id":549218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548775#post548775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when people are comparing Beasts to werewolves, they're seeing the wolves having to play in the Beast's strengths. Not surprisingly, since Beast the game is written from that perspective. In a hunt? The wolves are far better off. Always will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the Needs Must Atavism is pretty comparable to Werewolf Tracking with Low Satiety or a Satiety Expenditure.<br /> <br /> <b>Needs Must</b>: Add Lair dots to Perception rolls, including reaction to surprise. Ignores distance related penalties to Perception equal to Lair. Far senses with a moment of concentration. Instinctively senses when potential meal that would increase Satiety is nearby. Does not penetrate magical disguise or obfuscation.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety</b>: Mark target capable of raising Satiety, can track it anywhere regardless of distance and automatically succeeds on uncontested rolls to do so with rote quality on contested rolls to locate. Allows Clash of Wills against supernatural attempts to hide if target is marked first. Lose Mark if Satiety rises to 4 or more, can recover it if it drops again with Wits+Survival.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Can mark anyone or anything and track to the end of the earth, if marked target is living thing, can borrow its senses for Lair in minutes once per day.<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out I'm not claiming any of this is overpowered, I stand by my original statement <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548441#post548441\">here</a>. I'm just clarifying some of the capabilities of Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:21:18-07:00","id":549225,"title":"","content":"Game balance is an illusion, but only a fool doesn't look at various powers and realize certain splats have powers that run roughshod over others. Hell, they specifically call this out in the Vampire+Beast crossover section. Beast talks about being good for crossover, and the powers are simple enough to manage that in theory. But its clear, yet again in Second Edition, that Vampire and Werewolf have design goals that the rest of the splats do not have. Leading to things like Demon, Beast, and Mage popping out aggravated damage and jumping across worlds while Vampires have to frenzy to deal aggravated and Werewolves need a Locus to travel to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> So far the best bet is to make the fluff-based story as much as you want, but definitely don't bring the crunch of other gamelines into your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:22:14-07:00","id":549228,"title":"","content":"It takes up a power slot, so it makes sense it would be a bit stronger than something an entire splat gets for free. Werewolves can get facets that pump their tracking even further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:30:45-07:00","id":549238,"title":"","content":"As you can see from my quote, I wasn't commenting on the overall power of the ability, but more in reference to MCN's suggestion that wolves are far better off at the hunt. If a Beast decides to be a hunter, they can get better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:04:05-07:00","id":549330,"title":"","content":"*Begins to write a fetish that eats people's fears, storing instances of lunacy, which can be tossed at beasts to be devoured/drench them into it, and add Satiety to them to the possible point of Slumber*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:09:37-07:00","id":549337,"title":"","content":"Acrozatarim used, I think, Hunger Influence to drain a car's gas tank. I suppose you could use Fear Influence to fill up a Beast, too.<br /> <br /> 'It\u2019s rare, but not unheard of, for a Beast to take a spirit into her brood via Kinship bonds. The resulting relationship is less akin to the one between a pack and its totem than one between symbiotic species: the Beast feeds her Hungers, generating Essence that feeds the spirit, who uses its Numina and Influences to help the Beast feed her Hungers.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:39:37-07:00","id":549391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549218#post549218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the Needs Must Atavism is pretty comparable to Werewolf Tracking with Low Satiety or a Satiety Expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's more to hunting than just tracking or perception. Each of the five forms, for instance, has a different use in the Hunt. Each Auspice provides an aura-effect tied to hunting. And all that is innate to all werewolves before boosting it with powers or merits, of which there are many in WtF.<br /> <br /> The mere fact that we're talking about innate abilities as opposed to a power or merit flat out makes them better as a baseline. Werewolves just get better with more investment, while the Beast needs investment to be roughly as good at hunting as a baseline werewolf. So, while a Beast can become a very good hunter, the wolves still beat them out in that area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549225#post549225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game balance is an illusion, but only a fool doesn't look at various powers and realize certain splats have powers that run roughshod over others. Hell, they specifically call this out in the Vampire+Beast crossover section. Beast talks about being good for crossover, and the powers are simple enough to manage that in theory. But its clear, yet again in Second Edition, that Vampire and Werewolf have design goals that the rest of the splats do not have. Leading to things like Demon, Beast, and Mage popping out aggravated damage and jumping across worlds while Vampires have to frenzy to deal aggravated and Werewolves need a Locus to travel to the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm..... you do realize that werewolves don't need a locus to shadow hop? There are other ways. People really need to stop comparing a supernatural with certain powers to baseline innate abilities. The two don't match up. Vampires need specific powers to deal aggravated damage, same as any other game line; the frenzy thing is actually a BENEFIT, believe it or not - you can use claws without Final Deathing another vampire, which is actually pretty nice in VtR. Mages need Mastery in Arcana to deal aggravated, its not exactly easy for them. For Demon, there's one specific Exploit, which is basically risking Compromise to use, which is a major drawback; someone witnessing a body disintegrate from your gunshots isn't exactly a good way to call down the angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> People are creating a very specific instances of one supernatural, and then expecting a below-character-creation-level of another supernatural, and expecting them to be equal. If you give one side all the benefits and no drawback, and the other side none but all drawbacks, then <i>of course</i> they're going to be unequal. <br /> <br /> I'd say that this is nothing more than white room theorycrafting, but honestly, its not even that - at least white room makes some attempt at giving the two sides equal footing before comparing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-10-2015, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:43:01-07:00","id":549393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549391#post549391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's more to hunting than just tracking or perception. Each of the five forms, for instance, has a different use in the Hunt. Each Auspice provides an aura-effect tied to hunting. And all that is innate to all werewolves before boosting it with powers or merits, of which there are many in WtF.<br /> <br /> The mere fact that we're talking about innate abilities as opposed to a power or merit flat out makes them better as a baseline. Werewolves just get better with more investment, while the Beast needs investment to be roughly as good at hunting as a baseline werewolf. So, while a Beast can become a very good hunter, the wolves still beat them out in that area.<br /> <br /> Ummm..... you do realize that werewolves don't need a locus to shadow hop? There are other ways. People really need to stop comparing a supernatural with certain powers to baseline innate abilities. The two don't match up. Vampires need specific powers to deal aggravated damage, same as any other game line; the frenzy thing is actually a BENEFIT, believe it or not - you can use claws without Final Deathing another vampire, which is actually pretty nice in VtR. Mages need Mastery in Arcana to deal aggravated, its not exactly easy for them. For Demon, there's one specific Exploit, which is basically risking Compromise to use, which is a major drawback; someone witnessing a body disintegrate from your gunshots isn't exactly a good way to call down the angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm kind of tired of people creating very specific instances of one supernatural, and then expecting a below-character-creation-level of another supernatural, and expecting them to be equal. If you give one side all the benefits and no drawback, and the other side none but all drawbacks, then <i>of course</i> they're going to be unequal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, new mage only need 4 dots to deal Agg. Just sayin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:50:00-07:00","id":549398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=549391#post549391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's more to hunting than just tracking or perception. Each of the five forms, for instance, has a different use in the Hunt. Each Auspice provides an aura-effect tied to hunting. And all that is innate to all werewolves before boosting it with powers or merits, of which there are many in WtF.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, aspects of the various forms can also be replicated and surpassed with Atavisms. Werewolves use human and wolf forms to hide, while a Beast can turn invisible or hide in a crowd. Dalu is for the urban hunt, but a Beast doesn't really need an advantage there. Gauru does powerful damage and heals, also replicated by Atavisms, as well as offering a better version of urshul's tilt-inflicting abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mere fact that we're talking about innate abilities as opposed to a power or merit flat out makes them better as a baseline. Werewolves just get better with more investment, while the Beast needs investment to be roughly as good at hunting as a baseline werewolf. So, while a Beast can become a very good hunter, the wolves still beat them out in that area. </div> </div> </div>Again, to be fair and on point with your original statement, you said with the hunt, the wolves were always better off and always would be. A Beast with Needs Must is already far better at tracking than my werewolf is, with the added benefit that the Beast doesn't need to taste his blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People are creating a very specific instances of one supernatural, and then expecting a below-character-creation-level of another supernatural, and expecting them to be equal. If you give one side all the benefits and no drawback, and the other side none but all drawbacks, then <i>of course</i> they're going to be unequal.<br /> <br /> I'd say that this is nothing more than white room theorycrafting, but honestly, its not even that - at least white room makes some attempt at giving the two sides equal footing before comparing them. </div> </div> </div>It's not white room theory crafting or even creating specific instances at all. It's explaining an ability and what it does, primarily when those abilities are likely to be used in a, as the title of the thread suggests, Beast vs Werewolf encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:56:28-07:00","id":549405,"title":"","content":"The advantage is that a werewolf can potentially track someone they've never met. They just need their scent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:33:23-07:00","id":690987,"title":"","content":"Beast wins... I mean, at all. Hands down, Everything, that werewolves can do, Beasts can d o better (except of dealing with spirits, may be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:35:10-07:00","id":690990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=548935#post548935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be pretty difficult for a Beast to last more than a turn after being applied the Stunned tilt and then being dog-piled by the whole Uratha pack ready to devour it alive, inflicting massive dose of aggravated damage, while at the same time, grappling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when Uratha inflict aggravated damage by devouring for nonn-humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:42:02-07:00","id":690992,"title":"","content":"The <i>flesh</i> of a beast is human. That's all that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:52:27-07:00","id":690995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=690992#post690992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>flesh</i> of a beast is human. That's all that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... may be, if GM will be kind enough. But as I remember, werewolves can inflict aggrav. damage only for pure mortal by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:11:34-07:00","id":691018,"title":"","content":"The book itself mentions being able to do it to other werewolves. It should also work on mages, claimed and sin eaters, and possibly changelings but to be honest that one's a bit fuzzy. Beasts, however, are an astral spirit bound to a very much human body. Their soul may be all shiny and powerful, but an Uratha's inner wolf spirit cares not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:21:52-07:00","id":691027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691018#post691018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book itself mentions being able to do it to other werewolves. It should also work on mages, claimed and sin eaters, and possibly changelings but to be honest that one's a bit fuzzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Actually, werewolves standard methods to inflict aggravate damage (like those Rite) work only on another werewolves (that's what disappointed me about 2ed - werewolves are too weak for high-level fights)/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:43:18-07:00","id":691036,"title":"","content":"Mages are fundamentally human. That's always been a thing with them. But seriously &quot;Too weak for high-level fights&quot;? Are we reading the same book? One of the listed effects of a five-dot fetish is counting as a bane for things that don't normally suffer them. There's your aggravated damage right there. Add in Eviscerate or Crimson Spasm plus high levels of Slaughterer and Primal Strength and you can count on doing some serious damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T04:51:57-07:00","id":691044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691027#post691027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Actually, werewolves standard methods to inflict aggravate damage (like those Rite) work only on another werewolves (that's what disappointed me about 2ed - werewolves are too weak for high-level fights)/</div> </div> </div> </div>Where it says they can eat wolves for aggravated damage, that refers to werewolves.<br /> <br /> It would work on those things because those things are human, though I think a Claimed far along on its claiming, where it has mutated, might be an exception. Mages, beasts and sin-eaters are humans who have an attachment to something else, but are still human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T05:00:59-07:00","id":691046,"title":"","content":"For a claimed, I think it would logically depend on the rank of the spirit claiming them. If it's formed from a human, which takes aggravated damage, and a spirit 2 or more ranks below the werewolf, which also takes aggravated damage, I don't see why combined they wouldn't <i>still </i>take aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Also I think the bit where it mentions wolves means actual, normal wolves. The logical reasons for being able to do so to werewolves as well is that they are both human <i>and</i> wolf, but if that's not solid enough for you then it's also mentioned explicitly on page 285 under &quot;Cannibalism&quot;. Quote: &quot;eating from another Uratha causes potentially deadly aggravated damage&quot;. <br /> <br /> Seems pretty black and white there, if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-06-2015, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T05:06:15-07:00","id":691048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691044#post691044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where it says they can eat wolves for aggravated damage, that refers to werewolves.<br /> <br /> It would work on those things because those things are human, though I think a Claimed far along on its claiming, where it has mutated, might be an exception. Mages, beasts and sin-eaters are humans who have an attachment to something else, but are still human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, it's work only for those &quot;humans&quot; who have no Power Trait<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691036#post691036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are fundamentally human. That's always been a thing with them. But seriously &quot;Too weak for high-level fights&quot;? Are we reading the same book? One of the listed effects of a five-dot fetish is counting as a bane for things that don't normally suffer them. There's your aggravated damage right there. Add in Eviscerate or Crimson Spasm plus high levels of Slaughterer and Primal Strength and you can count on doing some serious damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> I prefer the aggravated damage gift (like, Savage Rending in 1st ed) instead of Crimson Spasm (I dislike how CS work - you spend turn for activation and its limited by time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 10-06-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T05:20:49-07:00","id":691053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691048#post691048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, it's work only for those &quot;humans&quot; who have no Power Trait</div> </div> </div> </div>WHY? I don't get you. On the one hand you're complaining werewolves are too weak, but on the other you're continually nerfing them with baseless assumptions. Throw the dogs a bone, dude. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691048#post691048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the aggravated damage gift (like, Savage Rending in 1st ed) instead of Crimson Spasm (I dislike how CS work - you spend turn for activation and its limited by time).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically it's limited by fuel, so if you get munching while it's active you could theoretically make it last indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-06-2015, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T05:37:01-07:00","id":691056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691053#post691053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHY? I don't get you. On the one hand you're complaining werewolves are too weak, but on the other you're continually nerfing them with baseless assumptions. Throw the dogs a bone, dude.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, technically it's limited by fuel, so if you get munching while it's active you could theoretically make it last indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) It's not my fault, that the rules aren't clear. Usually, &quot;human&quot; =&quot;mortal&quot;<br /> 2) I don't get you. I just think, that good old &quot;reflexively spend 1 Essence and deal aggravated damage (optionally: only while your char in Gauru)&quot; would be better, than this useless gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T06:06:45-07:00","id":691130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691056#post691056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It's not my fault, that the rules aren't clear. Usually, &quot;human&quot; =&quot;mortal&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If Werewolf had meant mortals only, it would have <i>said </i>mortals. There's nothing about a mage that makes them not count. Human flesh is human flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T06:17:16-07:00","id":691145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691056#post691056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1) It's not my fault, that the rules aren't clear. Usually, &quot;human&quot; =&quot;mortal&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The rules are pretty clear. If it's a human, you do aggravated. Mages are human. Vampires are not human anymore. Sin-Eaters are humans claimed by a geist. Prometheans aren't human at all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) I don't get you. I just think, that good old &quot;reflexively spend 1 Essence and deal aggravated damage (optionally: only while your char in Gauru)&quot; would be better, than this useless gift. </div> </div> </div>It's hardly a useless gift, in fact it has a lot more usage than Savage Rending, allowing you to boost several traits, from armor to weapon bonuses to Strength and Stamina. And the new way Essence works, you're not going to be burning through it nearly as fast as you would in the first edition, with many abilities activating on their own when you enter Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691046#post691046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a claimed, I think it would logically depend on the rank of the spirit claiming them. If it's formed from a human, which takes aggravated damage, and a spirit 2 or more ranks below the werewolf, which also takes aggravated damage, I don't see why combined they wouldn't <i>still </i>take aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see, yeah.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-06-2015, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T06:53:35-07:00","id":691187,"title":"","content":"Oh, OK. Maybe you right and it's good if you do. However, I still not sure that it's work for sin-eaters and beasts and for others &quot;humans&quot; who claimed by NOT the Shadow Realm spirits. Anyway, I would prefer something to deal aggrav. damage to vampire, than to sin-eater or mage (I recognize, that it's completely subjective)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 10-06-2015, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T06:59:03-07:00","id":691199,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, I can see why they made Crimson Spasm instant rather than reflexive. If it was reflexive it would be absolutely brutal. You could just switch modes on the fly to be whatever you needed at the time. Guy hard to hit? Buff strength. Next dude a slow armoured thing? Drop the strength buff, reactivate and put it all in weapons modifier. Oh shit, guy's got a gun? Armour time. <br /> <br /> It becomes less like a super mode and more like a swiss army knife. Which is cool, but perhaps a little <i>too </i>powerful. Although I now have an idea for a fetish an elder Rahu might develop...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:22:20-07:00","id":691235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691187#post691187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I would prefer something to deal aggrav. damage to vampire, than to sin-eater or mage (I recognize, that it's completely subjective)</div> </div> </div> </div>You have the Tongue of Flame gift facet to inflict aggravated damage on vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T09:46:44-07:00","id":691361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691235#post691235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have the Tongue of Flame gift facet to inflict aggravated damage on vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, you need at east Purity 5 and good dicepool, if you want to be a firebender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:04:28-07:00","id":691380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691361#post691361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, you need at east Purity 5 and good dicepool, if you want to be a firebender.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say, about 3-4. 5 is when you Mass Create. You don't need that much to manupulate fire in interesting and damaging ways.<br /> <br /> And if you're a combat werewolf or a Rahu Purity is gonna be your main go to anyways...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:26:46-07:00","id":691392,"title":"","content":"You already need 5 Renown to get your Crimson Spasm.<br /> <br /> But really any boost to Strength will give you a great chance to shoving a stake in, resulting in what is effectively an instant win.<br /> <br /> Or you could just sneak up on them during the daytime and bite their head off while they sleep.<br /> <br /> You're white rooming it so there's no limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-06-2015, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T12:39:12-07:00","id":691592,"title":"","content":"Just remember, a Beast doesn't even need an Atavism to kill Vampires, just a couple of flood lights, and the Blazing Light Lair Trait. Burning is too difficult to impose with any regularity, and Kindred and others with ways to downgrade mundane Agg won't easily be hurt by Corrosive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:00:09-07:00","id":692222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=691392#post691392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or you could just sneak up on them during the daytime and bite their head off while they sleep.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not manly way))) Of course, the best enemy is those who you can kill by backstab, without alarming and when he sleep... but I'd prefer to have opportunity to dominate in &quot;white room&quot;. Without &quot;aggrave. ability&quot;, werewolves don't look like they can do something except of sneak up and backstub. And I actually don't care about Beasts, Demons and (probably) Mages - who gonna be the high league of WoD 2.0, - but be weaker than vampires... eww. That's why I think the new Uratha are scum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:16:35-07:00","id":692236,"title":"","content":"Oh-my-god-you're-serious-let-me-laugh-even-harder.jpg<br /> <br /> Seriously though, werewolves are <i>really fucking good</i> at &quot;sneak up and backstab&quot;. It's the speciality of one fifth of them. Another fifth have ready access to fire, which requires exactly the same level of experience as a vampire does to get aggravated attacks. <br /> <br /> Look, you can disparage them all you want for not being able to handle a straight up fight but just know a) you're wrong and b) they have other, better ways of making an opponent dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-07-2015, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:45:50-07:00","id":692250,"title":"","content":"Vampires can use zerg-rush with ghouls/mass-embraced neonats/brainwashed mortals, they can raise Attributes with blood spending AND the high-level one can inflict aggravated damage. Yep, werewolves can create Wolfblooded by using Lunacy (but the process is totally random) and summon some spirits, and using totems for trait-boosting, but it doesn't seem to be the fair ratio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T05:04:49-07:00","id":692254,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's break this down.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692250#post692250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can use zerg-rush with ghouls/mass-embraced neonats/brainwashed mortals,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It costs a willpower to ghoul a mortal, a humanity dot to embrace a vampire, and a hell of a long time to brainwash a mortal to the point they wouldn't immediately snap out of the brainwashing and run away at the sight of a rampaging wolf monster. And once it's over what do you do with the survivors? Vampire society frown upon this sort of thing for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692250#post692250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they can raise Attributes with blood spending AND the high-level one can inflict aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can raise attributes bychanging form and the high-level ones can inflict aggravated damage. what's your point? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692250#post692250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, werewolves can create Wolfblooded by using Lunacy (but the process is totally random)</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a tactic they would ever employ. Ever. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692250#post692250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and summon some spirits, and using totems for trait-boosting, but it doesn't seem to be the fair ratio.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite agree. Some spirits can set things on fire whilst on the other side of the gauntlet. The vamps don't stand a chance. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T05:21:09-07:00","id":692264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692254#post692254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not really. It costs a willpower to ghoul a mortal, a humanity dot to embrace a vampire</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>...and all of this will be problems only for a low-ranged Kindred, who will got <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">volunteered to be the seers.</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692254#post692254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And once it's over what do you do with the survivors?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Finish them off.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692254#post692254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Werewolves can raise attributes bychanging form and the high-level ones can inflict aggravated damage. what's your point? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> that werewolves can't do it as much (about trait boost), and as good (werewolf can't just make his claws &quot;aggravated&quot;) as vampire.</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692254#post692254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This isn't a tactic they would ever employ. Ever. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So much the worse for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T05:34:45-07:00","id":692295,"title":"","content":"Even a vampire can't &quot;just&quot; make their claws aggravated. They need to frenzy to do that. And the crucial thing about trait buffing is that werewolves can do it for free, whereas vampires have to spend blood to do it. And every two dice they add to their traits is a wound they can't heal that turn. All a werewolf has to do is survive until they run dry. Once that happens, the vampire is in trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:30:58-07:00","id":692507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692222#post692222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolves don't look like they can do something except of sneak up and backstub.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize this is how wolves hunt inferior prey, correct? (Superior, read, bigger prey is run down by pack tactics)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692250#post692250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can use zerg-rush with ghouls/mass-embraced neonats/brainwashed mortals, they can raise Attributes with blood spending AND the high-level one can inflict aggravated damage. Yep, werewolves can create Wolfblooded by using Lunacy (but the process is totally random) and summon some spirits, and using totems for trait-boosting, but it doesn't seem to be the fair ratio.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;summon some spirits&quot; Or y'know, make the battlefield a complete fiery inferno with no downsides for their packs while vampires, ghouls and thralls roast to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 10-07-2015, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:31:39-07:00","id":692515,"title":"","content":"Well, what's true for fighting Kindred is also true for fighting Uratha: get them to overcommit their resources and they'll lose. Bring in a few team-mates to tank or draw out your opponents Essence/Vitae-fuelled attacks, then you drop Lethal Nightmares, damaging Lair Traits, or overcharged Atavisms to finish them off.<br /> <br /> It's more accurate to factor in numbers than try to solo these experiments, anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:38:12-07:00","id":692520,"title":"","content":"Kuruth means never having to worry by Lethal damage and virtually all your most gruesome Facets on all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:48:07-07:00","id":692523,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Lethal damage, don't werewolf claws and teeth now explicitly deal Lethal damage to Vampires? I don't have my book handy, but I could have sworn 2E calls that out specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T08:52:53-07:00","id":692526,"title":"","content":"Just teeth. Since the Barghest facet only works in canine forms (and gauru) as well step 1 in fighting a vamp is pretty much &quot;get furry&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:28:11-07:00","id":692668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692507#post692507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize this is how wolves hunt inferior prey, correct? (Superior, read, bigger prey is run down by pack tactics)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I just tired, that vampires is this &quot;inferior prey&quot; in pretty much every setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:29:52-07:00","id":692669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692523#post692523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Lethal damage, don't werewolf claws and teeth now explicitly deal Lethal damage to Vampires? I don't have my book handy, but I could have sworn 2E calls that out specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I remember in - in Gauru their claws do too. If it doesn't... Uratha are really pathetic<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T10:51:06-07:00","id":692721,"title":"","content":"Gauru teeth and claw attacks use the same pool, don't require a grapple, and have the same damage modifier. They're mechanically indistinguishable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T14:17:39-07:00","id":694193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=692669#post692669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As I remember in - in Gauru their claws do too. If it doesn't... Uratha are really pathetic<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In all forms, an Uratha deals unendurable Lethal damage with their bite (and claw) attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T05:45:55-07:00","id":694754,"title":"","content":"By RAW - no, claws didn't (although, I wish they did). However, Elfive is right - in Gauru there is no difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:37:28-07:00","id":694890,"title":"","content":"Yes, 'claws' deal bashing in human form unless you use the Quicksilver Flesh Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:43:33-07:00","id":694960,"title":"","content":"Wait, what? Are we talking about vampires or in general? Because they're pretty explicitly lethal to anything else and I don't think quicksilver flesh would help against vamps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:50:52-07:00","id":694963,"title":"","content":"In hishu form a werewolf's 'claws' don't do lethal damage, though their teeth do. Use of Quicksilver Flesh can grant you claws that do +1L damage in hishu form.<br /> <br /> TheBadWolf was just nitpicking, I just clarified. I'm pretty sure they're trolling, incidentally. Anyone who read the book or looked at werewolves as a whole or any of the 'werewolves vs' threads wouldn't be calling werewolf 'pathetic.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:53:33-07:00","id":695111,"title":"","content":"An this is why Vs threads should be ignored, they invariably turn into a pissing contest where people insult other splats for no reason other than to prove something meaningless (their point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:02:21-07:00","id":695423,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Behold My True Form is unendurable. Can't say the same for Limb from Limb, but the Tilts are still nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:43:02-07:00","id":695448,"title":"","content":"The mechanic of bashing damage to vampires really only comes into play because of that special rule vampires have that reduces nonmagical damage by one step of lethality. Werewolf claws and bite attacks by default do lethal damage, aggravated in some circumstances. If werewolf claws and bites counted as magical, they stay that way and don't get downgraded. If they werent' they do get downgraded. I'm fairly sure they don't get downgraded anyways<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, do you guys mean Dalu for werewolf claws? Because I can't find the entry for Hishu having claws. Interestingly enough, the wording for the ability that gives Dalu lethal damage for claw attacks only specificies humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what's &quot;unendurable&quot; and such about? I am quite curious; I don't recall seeing it before, I might have missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-09-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T17:21:36-07:00","id":695500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=695448#post695448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanic of bashing damage to vampires really only comes into play because of that special rule vampires have that reduces nonmagical damage by one step of lethality. Werewolf claws and bite attacks by default do lethal damage, aggravated in some circumstances. If werewolf claws and bites counted as magical, they stay that way and don't get downgraded. If they werent' they do get downgraded. I'm fairly sure they don't get downgraded anyways</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf teeth are lethal in any form, they pierce through vampire's resistance because a werewolf has the spirit of a predator in them. A combat spec'd werewolf in human form can conceivably kill a human with their bared teeth with ease. Their claws do get downgraded to bashing, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do you guys mean Dalu for werewolf claws? Because I can't find the entry for Hishu having claws. Interestingly enough, the wording for the ability that gives Dalu lethal damage for claw attacks only specificies humans. </div> </div> </div>That's why I said 'claws,' since it's really just human nails. Dalu do get claws, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-09-2015, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:21:28-07:00","id":695838,"title":"","content":"No claws in Hishu, just bite, and the bite in Hishu and Urhan are specifically called out as non magical. &quot;While it doesn't afford any trait benefits over what a human normally possesses, a Hishu Uratha is more human than and human, and blends into a crowd.&quot; &quot;In Urshul a werewolf is an enormous wolf. She is a living breathing creature. Her claws are made of keratin. Her teeth are made of enamel and dentine. Until she changes to another form, she is an exceptionally large, exceptionally powerful, entirely natural wolf.&quot; All from page 96.<br /> <br /> It's only the three intermediary forms that are magical in nature for the purposes of Vampirie's innate damage downgrading ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:32:58-07:00","id":695842,"title":"","content":"&quot;Uratha bite to kill. Their teeth carry the deadly resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As such, their bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources. Even in Hishu, a werewolf\u2019s bite causes lethal damage to vampires.&quot; - Werewolf The Forsaken 2nd Edition pg 98","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T04:43:12-07:00","id":695937,"title":"","content":"Uratha always carry the resonance of the predator, and their bite always counts as 'mystical' (for whatever that means to the prey) even in Hishu, and are specifically called out as causing lethal to vampires. <br /> <br /> And Hishu and Urshul are specifically not flagged as 'non magical'. Hishu gives +1 Perception and makes them blend into crowds better than humans. Urshul inflicts Lunacy and allows application of Tilts without targeted attacks. The paragraph cited on p96 about Urshul has been quoted here out of context. It's noting that all werewolf forms are 'natural' and aren't caused by some kind of dispel-able magic. Urshul is a bloody great wolf, with teeth of enamel and claws of keratin. A Mage can't counter spell the form, and you can't cast a ward against 'unnatural forms' to keep it out. It's as much a part of nature as Hishu and Urhan. <br /> <br /> As a general guide, specifically stated rules take precedence over flavour text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-10-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T07:50:57-07:00","id":696087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=695937#post695937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's noting that all werewolf forms are 'natural' and aren't caused by some kind of dispel-able magic. A Mage counter counter spell the form, and you can't cast a ward against 'unnatural forms' to keep it out. It's as much a part of nature as Hishu and Urhan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh wait, did you just contradict yourself with a typo? Did you mean a mage <i>can't</i> dispell the form because to the werewolf it is not an &quot;unnatural form&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T08:52:40-07:00","id":696135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=695937#post695937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha always carry the resonance of the predator, and their bite always counts as 'mystical' (for whatever that means to the prey) even in Hishu, and are specifically called out as causing lethal to vampires.<br /> <br /> And Hishu and Urshul are specifically not flagged as 'non magical'. Hishu gives +1 Perception and makes them blend into crowds better than humans. Urshul inflicts Lunacy and allows application of Tilts without targeted attacks. The paragraph cited on p96 about Urshul has been quoted here out of context. It's noting that all werewolf forms are 'natural' and aren't caused by some kind of dispel-able magic. Urshul is a bloody great wolf, with teeth of enamel and claws of keratin. A Mage counter counter spell the form, and you can't cast a ward against 'unnatural forms' to keep it out. It's as much a part of nature as Hishu and Urhan.<br /> <br /> As a general guide, specifically stated rules take precedence over flavour text.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can't counterspell it because it's not a spell, not because it's natural or unnatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T08:56:07-07:00","id":696138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=695448#post695448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanic of bashing damage to vampires really only comes into play because of that special rule vampires have that reduces nonmagical damage by one step of lethality. Werewolf claws and bite attacks by default do lethal damage, aggravated in some circumstances. If werewolf claws and bites counted as magical, they stay that way and don't get downgraded. If they werent' they do get downgraded. I'm fairly sure they don't get downgraded anyways<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, do you guys mean Dalu for werewolf claws? Because I can't find the entry for Hishu having claws. Interestingly enough, the wording for the ability that gives Dalu lethal damage for claw attacks only specificies humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what's &quot;unendurable&quot; and such about? I am quite curious; I don't recall seeing it before, I might have missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rule name for a Vampire's ability to downgrade damage is &quot;Kindred Endurance,&quot; so a shorthand for effects that specifically ignore that rule is &quot;unendurable.&quot; It's similar to referring to damage that a Mage can't heal magically as &quot;resistant damage.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T14:01:55-07:00","id":696475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=696087#post696087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh wait, did you just contradict yourself with a typo? Did you mean a mage <i>can't</i> dispell the form because to the werewolf it is not an &amp;quot;unnatural form&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, typo. Thanks, I've fixed it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T03:31:42-07:00","id":698479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=694963#post694963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TheBadWolf was just nitpicking, I just clarified. I'm pretty sure they're trolling, incidentally. Anyone who read the book or looked at werewolves as a whole or any of the 'werewolves vs' threads wouldn't be calling werewolf 'pathetic.'</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, no, I'm not. But, yep, this is smt like my &quot;trigger point&quot;, I admit it. I don't require balance for all. I really don't care,I do not care that werewolves suck compared to Demons and Beasts and they (probably) will suck compared to Mages. And they will be weaker <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(at least in combat) to</span></span></span> mummy and prometheans (as it was in 1st ed), hell, even if they will be weaker than sin-eaters and changelings - I'll accept it. But werewolves must be at least as powerful as vampires - that's my only require to them.. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T03:46:06-07:00","id":698487,"title":"","content":"Don't worry. They are. <br /> <br /> Here's how an all out war between vamps and wolves would go:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires: </b>&quot;OH GOD WHY IS EVERYTHING ON FIRE?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T07:00:07-07:00","id":698604,"title":"","content":"I just can't see how werewolves could be<i><b> weak.</b></i><br /> How can you compare two supernatural races ony by white rooms and combat power?<br /> <br /> Anyone thinking about possible <i>realistic</i> situation between a pack and another group of vampires/beast/mage ecc.?<br /> Even one werewolf with a couple of merits and gifts could be an hell of a challenge for any 1vs1 possible<i> fight </i>between realistic characters.<br /> New uratha are natural<i> born killers</i>.<br /> Hand to hand combat with werewolves, statistically, is suicide in the new edition. They are not unbeatable. But if you want to beat them in a fight, unless your characters are elder and powerful, <i>very powerful</i>, and the pack is not made of elder uratha, good luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-12-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T07:05:59-07:00","id":698608,"title":"","content":"It's not even a &quot;white rooms are bullshit&quot; problem. It's a &quot;Who the fuck taught this guy to white room?&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> Elder vamp vs elder werewolf. Ok. The vamp is on fire. The room is on fire. The werewolf is <i>somewhere </i>in the surrounding ten miles and everything between him and the vamp is <i>also on fire. </i>gg.<br /> <br /> Note that this is also the method for dealing with mummies, prometheans, and pretty much anything else, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T07:21:04-07:00","id":698614,"title":"","content":"I will also point out if your GM is planning on being a little extra liberal, you can Unmake a Demon since they are all machines. And there is technically no rule about using it on creatures especially demon.<br /> <br /> That's an instakilll. They can resist but the option and interpretation is there. <br /> <br /> In fact the other technology gifts theoretically do something nasty to demons. If you count them as machines.<br /> <br /> Also in a fight, I think everyone decided that a werewolf vs mage fight was too much of a toss up for there to be a clear winner","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-12-2015, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T07:39:59-07:00","id":698618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698614#post698614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also point out if your GM is planning on being a little extra liberal, you can Unmake a Demon since they are all machines. And there is technically no rule about using it on creatures especially demon.<br /> <br /> That's an instakilll. They can resist but the option and interpretation is there.<br /> <br /> In fact the other technology gifts theoretically do something nasty to demons. If you count them as machines.<br /> <br /> Also in a fight, I think everyone decided that a werewolf vs mage fight was too much of a toss up for there to be a clear winner</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll have to check Demon to see if that works. It may well be legit, in which case the Demon would still get to contest with Resolve + Power Stat but would then die, yes.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T08:04:58-07:00","id":698624,"title":"","content":"Oh right. I forgot to account for demons own core book. Well is there a section on specifically how technology manipulation works on demons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T08:53:48-07:00","id":698639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698614#post698614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also point out if your GM is planning on being a little extra liberal, you can Unmake a Demon since they are all machines. And there is technically no rule about using it on creatures especially demon.<br /> <br /> That's an instakilll. They can resist but the option and interpretation is there.<br /> <br /> In fact the other technology gifts theoretically do something nasty to demons. If you count them as machines.<br /> <br /> Also in a fight, I think everyone decided that a werewolf vs mage fight was too much of a toss up for there to be a clear winner</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh-key. I get that werewolves quite bad-ass, but here you go too far. As I remember this gift work only for mundane technology. GM must be <b>extremely </b>pro-werewolf to allow this trick. Anyway, I don't give a shift about demons or others. Vampires are my arc-nemesis (*cough* Yep, Underworld-series and Dresden Files caused irreparable damage to my psyche<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T09:06:51-07:00","id":698644,"title":"","content":"Just <i>hunt </i>them.<br /> If you want to beat a vampire playing his social game you're just fucked.<br /> Hunt and kill is why werewolves exist. Vampires cannot beat them playing the same game.<br /> Find them , track them, hunt them and butcher them/set them on fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> It actually work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-12-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T09:22:40-07:00","id":698654,"title":"","content":"Okay, I just have to ask. <i>Why</i> is the werewolf form so constantly plagued by Werweolf v. Something Else threads? Don't they get old? We're going to have the wofl fans suport the wolves, the vamp fans support the vamps, the beast fans the beasts, the demon fans the demons, the mage fnas the mages, etc. It comes down to the players and system mastery. That is all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T09:29:13-07:00","id":698658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698644#post698644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just <i>hunt </i>them.<br /> If you want to beat a vampire playing his social game you're just fucked.<br /> Hunt and kill is why werewolves exist. Vampires cannot beat them playing the same game.<br /> Find them , track them, hunt them and butcher them/set them on fire.<br /> It actually work.</div> </div> </div> </div> In oWoD, social games of vampires could be a HUGE problem for hunt. It's so easy to hunt when all city police looking for your ass, and all city mafia looking for your family. However, now werewolf seems not so helpless in social conflicts. They can't be compared with vampires, but IMO, they can block the vamps activity at least to buy some time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T09:42:09-07:00","id":698663,"title":"","content":"In fact, garou are <i>warriors</i>. Uratha are <i>hunter.</i><br /> The hunt is the basic concept of the uratha society and tribal identity.<br /> They do everything for the hunt because of their nature and because of their duty. So, the owod situation it's a totally different matter.<br /> The Nwod 2nd edition vampire power comes from social disciplines and vampire coven and social merits.<br /> For werewolves, well, they are not only brutal and efficent killers but they have also impressive social advantages, not for everything, but fort the <i>hunt. </i>Every form, merit and gift is for the hunt.<br /> <br /> So, Explaining again my point of view: follow the rules of the hunt and everything will die.<br /> I know, it's not simple as I say, but now, the new uratha are scary as hell if you are the prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:03:17-07:00","id":698699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698614#post698614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also point out if your GM is planning on being a little extra liberal, you can Unmake a Demon since they are all machines. And there is technically no rule about using it on creatures especially demon.<br /> <br /> That's an instakilll. They can resist but the option and interpretation is there.<br /> <br /> In fact the other technology gifts theoretically do something nasty to demons. If you count them as machines.<br /> <br /> Also in a fight, I think everyone decided that a werewolf vs mage fight was too much of a toss up for there to be a clear winner</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No, they're not. They're bio-mechanical spiritual-entities-made-material-but-still-partially-quantum-spirits. They are immensely more complicated than just machines.<br /> <br /> 2) Any fight between anything is a toss up because without a definite scenario, nothing can truly be determined.<br /> <br /> As for Bad and his underselling of Werewolves...<br /> <br /> 1) Minor personal complaint, I just think the entire werewolf/vampire rivalry is lame.<br /> <br /> 2) Werewolves are masters of the physical senses and therefore tracking, controllling the environment, and stripping their targets of exterior blessings down to their simple brute nature. Vampires are masters of senses within the dark and for the living, uninhibited by the former and keenly aware of blood and beating hearts at pretty much all time. They are also masters of controlling social environments and people and making themselves necessary to others. It comes down whether vampires can utilize the darkness of men to conquer their world and/or personally self-master themselves to keep pace with a werewolves many aggressive personal abilities. It's fairly even without context.<br /> <br /> And on the upfront topic:<br /> <br /> Beasts are masters of creating the environment, werewolves are masters of manipulating and subverting it. Beasts have perpetual active skills that flux in regard to their feeding, werewolves have several &quot;Slam for breaking&quot; powers that are consistent. It's tough to call, because in many ways they are diametrically opposed-beast creates walls, werewolves bring walls down. Without context, it's impossible to tell.<br /> <br /> One major factor is if a werewolf can affect a beast's Lair, but I'm assuming not and calling it a draw. If a werewolf can turn a Lair against the beast, then they have a markedly increased advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:03:44-07:00","id":698701,"title":"","content":"Short version: If you're fighting a supernatural creature on their own terms, you're gonna lose. Don't take a Werewolf head-on, don't try to outmaneuver Vampires, don't try to outlast a Sin-Eater, and never go after a Changeling if he knows you're coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:15:01-07:00","id":698710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698639#post698639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh-key. I get that werewolves quite bad-ass, but here you go too far. As I remember this gift work only for mundane technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually doesn't say that. The issue is that it says it targets a device. I asked in another thread for opinions but only got one response, in the negative. They didn't think angels were devices, but by definition, they are things made or adapted for a specific purpose. Demons aren't fulfilling their purpose, but they were still made by the God Machine for a specific task. The issue with them is more that they might not be considered technology, which has to be based in science, while angels and demons straddle the fence between technology and magic.<br /> <br /> The thing is, you say shit like 'werewolves are pathetic' on the werewolf board, and 'werewolves can't be compared with vampires or anyone else,' and repeatedly ignore numerous people showing you how they aren't pathetic and can be comparable to them, just complaining more and more. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656919#post656919\">Even the mage developer thinks a werewolf would beat a mage</a>, providing the mage didn't prep the battlefield or something.<br /> <br /> As for why, MCN, I think it's two things. One is as Helur pointed out, there's a lot of people who see Forsaken as an extension of Apocalypse, and expect Uratha to be like Garou, even using the same terms. In Apocalypse, they were warriors and constantly did aggravated to vampires and all sorts of ripping and tearing, and when the Uratha don't walk around everywhere in 'war form' and passively inflict aggravated damage to everyone they look at, people start whinging over them not having things like the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=584984#post584984\">First Class</a> merit.<br /> <br /> The other thing is that some of us more long-term fans are used to werewolves being little better than mortal occultists or psychics. First edition had some nice abilities but compared to every other splat they were nothing. Second edition has not only drastically changed that, but given them a purpose that could have them played like Hunter, where packs actively hunt and fight other supernatural beings. So when people say something like, 'such and such would always beat a werewolf,' while that may have been true in first edition, it certainly isn't as absolute in second, and this being a forum for discussion, we'll point that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:15:14-07:00","id":698712,"title":"","content":"Technically, the qualifiers of &quot;machine&quot; don't neccesarily mean has to be digital or not magical. Still, it's mostly just a funny idea if the GM is willing to stretch the idea to include demons. I know perfectly well it's not the intention of the technology gifts... but you gotta admit, the kinds of hilarity that would happen as a result of it being a valid interpretation are too funny to pass up in certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Arc, you're forgetting all of the built in Teamplay werewolves have. While I am sure vampires have their own synergies when working together, werewolves I think have a whole lot more mileage in terms of group buffing. Especially with Totems with the right bonuses.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:21:23-07:00","id":698719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698624#post698624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh right. I forgot to account for demons own core book. Well is there a section on specifically how technology manipulation works on demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but there is the bit where they're rogue constructs of sufficiently-advanced magic who can instantiate a complete human body out of a fistful of napkins and a few ccs of blood and treat their Integrity-equivalent as a powerstat while so ensconced. Oh, and <i>not objects, items, devices, or &quot;piece[s] of significant engineering&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Allowing Unmake to apply to demons requires logic that extends its list of viable targets to <i>humans</i>, because if a sapient pillar of fire and bone counts as technology then there's nothing stopping a body that actually adheres to known mechanical principles from also qualifying.<br /> <br /> No matter how they're put together, the Unchained aren't robots. They're formerly angels, currently demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T10:32:29-07:00","id":698724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=698699#post698699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on the upfront topic:<br /> <br /> Beasts are masters of creating the environment, werewolves are masters of manipulating and subverting it. Beasts have perpetual active skills that flux in regard to their feeding, werewolves have several &quot;Slam for breaking&quot; powers that are consistent. It's tough to call, because in many ways they are diametrically opposed-beast creates walls, werewolves bring walls down. Without context, it's impossible to tell.<br /> <br /> One major factor is if a werewolf can affect a beast's Lair, but I'm assuming not and calling it a draw. If a werewolf can turn a Lair against the beast, then they have a markedly increased advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div> A few thoughts - Beasts create and mainpulate the ultimate Safe Place, while werewolves manipulate wider territories. In vampire terms, its the difference between one's haven and one's feeding grounds. The scopes of their abilities, while both tied to surroundings, are pretty much completely different. So, its not like we're generally talking about environment against environment here. Werewolves have their defined grounds that give them wider scope, while Beasts have a literal home field advantage inside their Lair, not in random places. Beasts generally have difficulty opening their Lair outside of certain locations, so its not like we can have random comparisons.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the Astral Realms book seems to suggest that werewolves can feed on &quot;astral spirits&quot; like normal. And powers in the Astral tend to work the same as in reality. While it might be different in 2e, so far it seems to indicate that there's nothing unique about the Lair that can't be manipulated by Gifts. So, I see no reason a werewolf's abilities wouldn't work in the Lair. That said, Beasts are immune to environmental effects that resonate with the Lair, so its impossible to turn the Lair's environement against a Beast. Just doesn't work that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:26:07-07:00","id":698976,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figured that.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day though, it's the same song and dance. we're conflicting two entire worlds, and it just doesn't parse out in any cohesively clear manner.<br /> <br /> VS Threads don't help anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:26:56-08:00","id":772489,"title":"","content":"I was not sure how powerful Beasts would be, especially considering the generous regeneration that werewolves now have, but tinkering a bit I thought of the following build<br /> <br /> Beast would be an <u>Ugallu</u><br /> <br /> Hunger would be <u>Prey</u><br /> <br /> Avatisms: <u>Eye of Heaven, Wings of the Raptor</u><br /> <br /> Nightmares: <u>You are not alone, You cannot run</u><br /> <br /> If you have a bit of experience, or start off a bit more experienced (around the block for 5 bonus points), get the Avitism <u>Limb from Limb</u>. <br /> <br /> So, with this build the Beast can perch on a building and search for werewolves with her eagle eyes. Once she has found her prey, she can swoop down and deliver a devastating airborne attack. Combined with Limb from Limb, this will be enhanced and can even be aggravated. The werewolf might be frozen and unaware through the use of nightmares (you are not alone, you cannot run). If the attack is from a high up place like a building, the werewolf will be dead meat. This build could surely collect a number of werewolf pelts to satisfy her hunger for prey and show the world who the top predator is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:57:02-08:00","id":772506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=772489#post772489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with this build the Beast can perch on a building and search for werewolves with her eagle eyes. Once she has found her prey, she can swoop down and deliver a devastating airborne attack. Combined with Limb from Limb, this will be enhanced and can even be aggravated. The werewolf might be frozen and unaware through the use of nightmares (you are not alone, you cannot run). If the attack is from a high up place like a building, the werewolf will be dead meat. This build could surely collect a number of werewolf pelts to satisfy her hunger for prey and show the world who the top predator is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside how the rules for Nightmares make that &quot;frozen <i>or</i> unaware,&quot; you're relying on High Satiety effects in conjunction with Low Satiety effects and Satiety Expenditure effects and assuming that the character has the level of vision required to pick out an individual human-sized being from high up enough to make Wings of the Raptor's dive attack bonus large enough to eat the target's entire Health without having Needs Must.<br /> <br /> Also this build is stymied by staying indoors or under trees, this hypothetical assumes a werewolf without the capacity to shapeshift reflexively into a form with more Health, and this exploit assumes that the &quot;if you have a means of dealing lethal damage then the entire attack converts to lethal damage&quot; aspect of the dive combines with Limb From Limb's &quot;make your next attack deal aggravated damage&quot; effect in a particular fashion against supernatural opponents.<br /> <br /> This really isn't a useful exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T13:10:51-08:00","id":773364,"title":"","content":"As someone with only passing familiarity with beadt, how does the build fail?<br /> <br /> As far as i can gather, the combination has conditions that conflict with their ordering, making the attack as given literally impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, that's a sneak attack... anyone who sets up the sneak attack has advantage exploiting it and thus oneshotting the oponent. As I recall, there's ways for a werewolf to do that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:31:01-08:00","id":773466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/548379-beast-vs-werewolf?p=773364#post773364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that's a sneak attack... anyone who sets up the sneak attack has advantage exploiting it and thus oneshotting the oponent. As I recall, there's ways for a werewolf to do that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple times in a scene and with each subsequent successful sneaking around, makes it even harder to counter. With a given werewolf's healing, it's quite possible to set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:58:41-08:00","id":773747,"title":"","content":"Beast: *Uses You Cannot Run*<br /> <br /> Werewolf:*Vanishes, consumed by a need to hide.*<br /> <br /> Beast &quot;Where the fuck did he go?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}